I would get the Windows port of bash [it comes with MSYS, available from
http://www.mingw.org/, I believe] and use the following batch file:

@echo off

C:
chdir C:\cygwin\bin

bash --login -i

where C:\cygwin\bin is your binary. Net result is that I don't have
Nethack taking up half the screen, and it otherwise behaves like Nethack
in a terminal on Linux. [Note I mean the console, not xterm or
gnome-terminal or konsole.]

